   <p>Browse by price, rating, or how many reviews each style has, and click through to Amazon for the full size chart and current availability.</p>''', '[{"items": [{"a": "Look for interlock knit constructions rather than jersey knits. Interlock fabrics weave two layers together, providing exceptional opacity and preventing the fabric from thinning out when stretched.", "q": "What fabric features prevent plus-size leggings from going sheer over the hips?"}, {"a": "Prioritize a wide, curved waistband that matches the natural anatomy of your hips, or look for styles featuring an inner drawstring or high-recovery elastane that holds its shape.", "q": "How do I choose leggings that won''t slide down throughout the day?"}, {"a": "Seek out styles with flatlock seams or seamless inner thighs to eliminate friction points. High-quality nylon-spandex blends wick moisture quickly, reducing the dampness that aggravates chafing.", "q": "What are the best plus-size leggings for preventing inner thigh chafing?"}], "title": ""}, {"items": [{"a": "Not necessarily. True compression gear is designed to feel snug. Sizing up can cause the fabric to bunch, wrinkle, and lose its supportive benefits, leading to sliding. Follow the hip measurements on the size chart.", "q": "Should I size up in compression leggings for a more comfortable fit?"}, {"a": "Brushed polyester-spandex blends are incredibly comfortable for lounging and yoga, but friction from gym equipment or cardio can cause them to pill. Opt for smooth, slick technical fabrics for intense workouts.", "q": "Are brushed \"buttery soft\" leggings durable enough for high-intensity gym sessions? "}, {"a": "A 7/8 length inseam is slightly shorter than full length, sitting just above the ankle bone. For many petite plus-size individuals, this cut fits perfectly as a full-length option without bunching at the bottom.", "q": "What is a 7/8 length legging, and how does it fit a plus-size frame?"}], "title": ""}]'),
	('e129f184-5985-4aed-a86e-9b8f5c3f2ff2', 'High Waisted Leggings', 'High Waisted Leggings', 'https://vptbrllldcvgykpfljjd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/admin-uploads/general/1782410282594-r82c02.jpg', 3, true, '2026-06-24 01:49:21.332601+00', '2026-07-01 00:27:05.776+00', 'A great pair of high-waisted leggings offers more than a flattering silhouette, they provide the support and confidence you need to move comfortably throughout the day. Loved for their secure fit and extra coverage, high-waisted styles stay in place during workouts while creating a smooth, streamlined look. We''ve rounded up some of the best high-waisted leggings for women, featuring premium fabrics, squat-proof construction, moisture-wicking performance, and all-day comfort. Whether you''re heading to the gym, practicing yoga, or styling them for everyday wear, these leggings are designed to perform as beautifully as they look.', '[{"items": [{"a": "High-waisted leggings sit above the natural waist, usually between the navel and ribcage. This gives extra core coverage, helps keep the waistband in place during movement, and creates a smoother, more supportive fit compared to mid-rise or low-rise styles.", "q": "What makes high-waisted leggings different from regular leggings?"}, {"a": "Yes, the higher waistband stays put during squats, lunges, and other high-intensity movements without rolling down. Look for styles with four-way stretch fabric and moisture-wicking properties for the best workout performance.", "q": "Are high-waisted leggings good for working out?"}, {"a": "Check customer reviews and photos on the product listing — reviewers almost always mention opacity during movement. Darker colours and thicker fabrics tend to perform better, but real-world feedback from verified buyers is the most reliable indicator.", "q": "How do I know if high-waisted leggings will be squat-proof?"}], "title": ""}, {"items": [{"a": "Absolutely. Many women wear high-waisted leggings as everyday bottoms paired with oversized tops, blazers, or tunics. Styles in solid colours or subtle textures tend to transition most easily from gym to daily wear.", "q": "Can high-waisted leggings be worn casually, not just for exercise?"}, {"a": "Sizing varies by brand, so always check the size chart on the product listing before ordering. If you''re between sizes, reviews mentioning fit and stretch can help — many brands note whether their leggings run true to size, small, or large.", "q": "What size should I choose for high-waisted leggings?"}, {"a": "Yes, many brands offer high-waisted leggings in extended sizes specifically designed for a comfortable, secure fit at every size. The high waistband is particularly flattering for plus-size body types, offering extra support without digging in. Always check the size range listed on the product page before buying.", "q": "Are high-waisted leggings suitable for plus-size women?"}], "title": ""}]'),
	('c9783a0f-86fb-48a7-9a2a-dde0595d5560', 'Workout Leggings', 'Workout Leggings', 'https://vptbrllldcvgykpfljjd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/admin-uploads/general/1782410419083-nctwhn.jpg', 6, true, '2026-06-24 01:49:21.332601+00', '2026-07-01 22:54:11.312+00', NULL, '[{"items": [{"a": "Synthetic fibers like nylon and polyester pull sweat away from your skin to the fabric''s surface, where it evaporates quickly, keeping you cool, dry, and free from sweat rashes.", "q": "Why is moisture-wicking fabric essential for high-intensity training?"}, {"a": "Flatlock seams join fabric edges flat against each other without bulk. This significantly minimizes chafing and skin raw spots caused by repetitive motion during running or lifting.", "q": "What is the benefit of flatlock seams in athletic apparel?"}, {"a": "High-quality activewear integrates reinforced stitching around mesh or fabric panels, allowing pockets to expand for a smartphone without compromising the overall hold or sliding down.", "q": "Do side drop-in pockets affect the compression of gym leggings?"}], "title": ""}, {"items": [{"a": "With regular use (2-3 times a week), high-performance leggings typically last 1 to 2 years. Replace them when you notice bagging at the knees, loose threads along structural seams, or a loss of waistband elasticity.", "q": "How often should you replace performance workout leggings?"}, {"a": "Running leggings work, but they often feature back zippers for keys that can dig into your spine during bench presses or floor work. Pure training leggings prioritize flat, hardware-free surfaces.", "q": "Can you wear running leggings for heavy weightlifting sessions?"}, {"a": "It means the fabric remains completely opaque when stretched. Stand in front of a well-lit mirror, perform a deep squat, and check if your undergarments or skin show through the seat of the pants.", "q": "What does \"squat-proof\" mean, and how do I test it at home?"}], "title": ""}]'),
	('41eca6ec-cad0-4a39-b77f-90916bb77be6', 'Capri Leggings', 'Capri Leggings', 'https://vptbrllldcvgykpfljjd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/admin-uploads/general/1782491314419-lde0pl.jpg', 8, false, '2026-06-24 01:49:21.332601+00', '2026-07-01 23:40:07.944+00', NULL, '[{"items": [{"a": "Classic capri leggings should land mid-calf, right around the widest part of your lower leg. If you prefer a slightly longer line, look for crop lengths that hit just below the calf.", "q": "Where should capri leggings ideally hit on the leg?"}, {"a": "Yes, the cropped length exposes the lower leg and ankle, allowing for better heat dissipation and air circulation during outdoor summer runs or humid gym sessions.", "q": "Are capri workout pants better than full-length leggings for summer?"}, {"a": "Look for styles with wide, raw-cut, or laser-cut leg openings rather than tight, elasticated stitched cuffs. A softer fabric blend with multi-way stretch will also prevent constriction.", "q": "How do I stop capri leggings from digging into my calves?"}], "title": ""}, {"items": [{"a": "Because they visually break up the leg line at the calf, they can shorten the silhouette slightly. To counter this, style them with a matching high-waisted sports bra or crop top to elongate your midsection.", "q": "Do capri leggings make you look shorter?"}, {"a": "They are exceptionally versatile, making them ideal for indoor cycling (keeping fabric away from the bike chain), yoga, barre, Pilates, and casual warm-weather errands.", "q": "What activities are cropped capri leggings best suited for?"}, {"a": "Yes, they pair well. You can pull compression socks up to meet the hem of the capris, making them an excellent combo for recovery or long-distance running.", "q": "Can you wear compression socks with capri gym leggings?"}], "title": ""}]'),
	('a0415f1b-0c10-4b27-9474-4d0bce67f94a', 'Scrunch Shorts', 'Scrunch Shorts', 'https://vptbrllldcvgykpfljjd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/admin-uploads/general/1782948628436-vaxrhn.jpg', 9, true, '2026-07-01 23:14:43.304705+00', '2026-07-01 23:30:31.083+00', 'Scrunch shorts feature a gathered seam at the back that enhances your natural shape while maintaining comfort during movement.', '[{"items": [{"a": "The vertical ruched \"scrunch\" stitching runs down the center back seam, acting to separate and accentuate the glute muscles, creating a highly contoured, rounder aesthetic appearance.", "q": "What is the purpose of the ruched seam on scrunch shorts?"}, {"a": "When properly sized, high-quality seamless scrunch shorts expand with your body and shouldn''t cause discomfort. If it feels restrictive or digs in, it''s a clear sign you need to size up.", "q": "Does the scrunch seam feel uncomfortable or irritating during workouts?"}, {"a": "Look for heavy-duty reinforcement or four-needle six-thread flatlock stitching. Poorly made varieties can pop under heavy load, so investing in premium seamless brands is essential for heavy leg days.", "q": "Is the gathered stitching on glute-contouring shorts prone to tearing?"}], "title": ""}, {"items": [{"a": "Many fitness enthusiasts prefer sizing up by one size because the ruching takes up some fabric length, and a slightly looser fit ensures the seam sits perfectly in the gluteal fold without overstretching.", "q": "Should I size up when ordering seamless scrunch gym shorts?"}, {"a": "They are highly popular in modern weightlifting and bodybuilding communities. If modesty is a priority, opting for a darker color or a slightly longer 5-inch inseam version offers a more subtle look.", "q": "Are scrunch butt shorts suitable for public commercial gym environments?"}, {"a": "Place them inside a mesh laundry bag, wash with cool water on a delicate cycle, and lay them flat to dry. High heat from a tumble dryer can degrade the elastic threads that create the scrunch effect.", "q": "How do I wash scrunch shorts to preserve the elastic gathering?"}], "title": ""}]'),
	('4e7220f0-b4bf-4ac3-8b0e-ff8f5d922955', 'Fleece Leggings', 'Fleece Leggings', 'https://vptbrllldcvgykpfljjd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/admin-uploads/general/1782948397635-thfuys.jpg', 10, true, '2026-07-01 23:26:43.406266+00', '2026-07-01 23:26:51.092+00', 'Designed with soft thermal lining, they provide warmth without adding bulk, making them perfect for winter workouts, outdoor walks, or cozy everyday wear. This selection includes top-rated fleece leggings featuring stretch fabrics, supportive high-rise waistbands, and insulating interiors that keep you warm and comfortable.', '[{"items": [{"a": "High-quality thermal fleece leggings with a wind-resistant nylon exterior can comfortably be worn alone down to freezing temperatures (32°F/0°C). For sub-zero conditions, they work perfectly as a base layer under shell pants.", "q": "Can fleece-lined leggings be worn as standalone pants in freezing weather?"}, {"a": " Modern tech-fleece variants utilize microfleece linings, which provide substantial thermal insulation with minimal thickness, keeping the sleek silhouette of traditional leggings.", "q": "Do fleece-insulated leggings make your legs look bulky?"}, {"a": "Look specifically for active-performance fleece leggings made from polyester-spandex blends. They offer brushed interiors for warmth while pulling moisture away to prevent chilling from dried sweat.", "q": "Are winter thermal leggings breathable enough for outdoor running?"}], "title": ""}, {"items": [{"a": "Wash them inside out, separate from items that shed lint (like cotton sweatshirts or towels), and avoid fabric softeners. Air drying keeps the face fabric smooth and pill-free.", "q": "How do I prevent lint and pilling on the exterior of my fleece leggings?"}, {"a": "A high, wide waistband with an internal elastic core is best. Because fleece-lined fabrics are inherently heavier than standard summer knits, a structured waist prevents them from sagging over time.", "q": "What waistband design is best for heavy thermal winter leggings?"}, {"a": "Polyester is far superior. Brushed polyester fleece traps warm air efficiently and handles moisture well, whereas cotton fleece absorbs dampness, loses its shape, and feels cold against the skin once wet.", "q": "Is polyester or cotton better for a fleece-lined legging interior?"}], "title": ""}]');


